==Trivia ==
*The Evolved Skeleton Army may be based on the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Immortals_(Achaemenid_Empire) Immortals], a legion in the Achaemenid Persian Army where their numbers would not decrease with its defeat, due to the casualties being replaced. It could also be inspired by the [[lotr:Dead_Men_of_Dunharrow|Dead Man of Dunharrow]] from The Lord Of The Rings, a ghost skeleton army that could attack but not be hit themselves, with the general representing the [[lotr:King_of_the_Dead|King of the Dead]].
*The Skeleton Army Evolution summons 15 Skeletons alongside General Gerry (16 skeletons in total), but as revealed in the [[Version History#Balance Changes (1/10/2018)|1/10/2018 balance changes]], one of the Skeletons in the regular Skeleton Army card is already named Gerry, which means that either another Skeleton called Gerry joined the army and became the general or the existing Gerry was promoted and an extra unnamed Skeleton replaced him.
*Before the Skeleton Army's Evolution's release, the Skeletons' attack time interval was increased to 1.1 seconds (from 1 second).
*It is possible to trap General Gerry in the back behind the player's King Tower via Hero Musketeer or Hero Bowler's ability. This allows the shadows to advance without almost any risk of them being killed due to Gerry being pretty much unreachable. The only way to kill General Gerry is to use spells against him (which will lead to the player's King Tower being activated) or to wait until the ability's effect expires in order to use spells safely (but by that point too much damage will have been done by the shadows).

